	/* Flush pending rcuog wakeup before the last need_resched() check */
	rcu_nocb_flush_deferred_wakeup();
```
Reason:
The unnecessary calls to `rcu_nocb_flush_deferred_wakeup()` during user and guest mode transitions lead to performance regressions when the nohz_full feature is not active on the local CPU. This results in the system polling for RCU wakeups that are not needed, causing a -3% performance hit.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
		/* Check if any of the above work has queued a deferred wakeup */
		tick_nohz_user_enter_prepare();
```
```c
	/* Flush pending rcuog wakeup before the last need_resched() check */
	tick_nohz_user_enter_prepare();
```
Reason:
The replacement of `rcu_nocb_flush_deferred_wakeup()` with `tick_nohz_user_enter_prepare()` ensures that the system only processes necessary wakeups relevant to the nohz_full feature, thus preventing unnecessary performance degradation during user and guest mode transitions.


